---@class aws.transcribe_streaming.StartCallAnalyticsStreamTranscriptionRequest
---@field LanguageCode? aws.transcribe_streaming.CallAnalyticsLanguageCode|string Specify the language code that represents the language spoken in your audio.
---@field MediaSampleRateHertz aws.transcribe_streaming.MediaSampleRateHertz The sample rate of the input audio (in hertz). Low-quality audio, such as telephone audio, is typically around 8,000 Hz. High-quality audio typically ranges from 16,000 Hz to 48,000 Hz. Note that the sample rate you specify must match that of your audio.
---@field MediaEncoding aws.transcribe_streaming.MediaEncoding|string Specify the encoding of your input audio. Supported formats are:
---@field VocabularyName? aws.transcribe_streaming.VocabularyName Specify the name of the custom vocabulary that you want to use when processing your transcription. Note that vocabulary names are case sensitive.
---@field SessionId? aws.transcribe_streaming.SessionId Specify a name for your Call Analytics transcription session. If you don't include this parameter in your request, Amazon Transcribe generates an ID and returns it in the response.
---@field AudioStream aws.transcribe_streaming.AudioStream An encoded stream of audio blobs. Audio streams are encoded as either HTTP/2 or WebSocket data frames.
---@field VocabularyFilterName? aws.transcribe_streaming.VocabularyFilterName Specify the name of the custom vocabulary filter that you want to use when processing your transcription. Note that vocabulary filter names are case sensitive.
---@field VocabularyFilterMethod? aws.transcribe_streaming.VocabularyFilterMethod|string Specify how you want your vocabulary filter applied to your transcript.
---@field LanguageModelName? aws.transcribe_streaming.ModelName Specify the name of the custom language model that you want to use when processing your transcription. Note that language model names are case sensitive.
---@field IdentifyLanguage? aws.transcribe_streaming.Boolean Enables automatic language identification for your Call Analytics transcription.
---@field LanguageOptions? aws.transcribe_streaming.LanguageOptions Specify two or more language codes that represent the languages you think may be present in your media.
---@field PreferredLanguage? aws.transcribe_streaming.CallAnalyticsLanguageCode|string Specify a preferred language from the subset of languages codes you specified in LanguageOptions.
---@field VocabularyNames? aws.transcribe_streaming.VocabularyNames Specify the names of the custom vocabularies that you want to use when processing your Call Analytics transcription. Note that vocabulary names are case sensitive.
---@field VocabularyFilterNames? aws.transcribe_streaming.VocabularyFilterNames Specify the names of the custom vocabulary filters that you want to use when processing your Call Analytics transcription. Note that vocabulary filter names are case sensitive.
---@field EnablePartialResultsStabilization? aws.transcribe_streaming.Boolean Enables partial result stabilization for your transcription. Partial result stabilization can reduce latency in your output, but may impact accuracy. For more information, see Partial-result stabilization.
---@field PartialResultsStability? aws.transcribe_streaming.PartialResultsStability|string Specify the level of stability to use when you enable partial results stabilization (EnablePartialResultsStabilization).
---@field ContentIdentificationType? aws.transcribe_streaming.ContentIdentificationType|string Labels all personally identifiable information (PII) identified in your transcript.
---@field ContentRedactionType? aws.transcribe_streaming.ContentRedactionType|string Redacts all personally identifiable information (PII) identified in your transcript.
---@field PiiEntityTypes? aws.transcribe_streaming.PiiEntityTypes Specify which types of personally identifiable information (PII) you want to redact in your transcript. You can include as many types as you'd like, or you can select ALL.

